From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Juanesf <juanesf91@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] sunxi: a733: reset the FE1.1S hub via VBUSM (PM5) in the SPL

The Radxa Cubie A7A has an FE1.1S USB 2.0 hub (U6) on the third USB2
PHY (USB2-DP/DM, balls C36/B37), i.e. the DWC3/xHCI upstream port. The
hub is strapped self-powered (BUSJ=1 via R61) and therefore uses VBUSM
(pin 16) as its upstream VBUS detector: a low level makes it drop the
1.5k pull-up on DPU and restart the upstream link state machine, even
though VD33 (DCDC1 via R58) and VDD5 (VCC5V0_SYS via FB3) are always
present. VBUSM is driven by USB_HOST_EN (PM5, ball N36) through R59;
the same PM5 also enables U5 (VCC5V0_USB20).

The vendor boot0 starts with PM5 low, so the hub sees a 0->1 edge on
VBUSM at power-on and presents its D+ pull-up. The mainline SPL
inherits PM5 high and never produces that edge: the xHCI USB2 port
stays CCS=0 and neither the hub (1a40:0101) nor the AIC8800 behind it
(a69c:8d81) enumerate. This reproduces on both our 7.4 port and on
Jernej's a733-display-wip tree with all VBUS regulators enabled.

Reproduce the edge at the earliest safe point: right after the AXP8191
probe in sunxi_pmic_init_a733(), while the R_PIO bank is already
clocked and long before U-Boot or Linux probe the DWC3. Drive PM5 low
for 30 ms, then high again. No SoC/PMIC rail is touched.

NOTE: cycling DCDC1 is deliberately NOT used. DCDC1 also feeds VCC-PL
(via R110), which powers PL0/PL1 (S-TWI0) - the very I2C bus used to
talk to the AXP318 - and SWOUT1/SWOUT2; dropping it would hang the SPL.

Signed-off-by: Juanesf <juanesf91@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 arch/arm/mach-sunxi/dram_sun60i_a733.c | 33 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 33 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/dram_sun60i_a733.c b/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/dram_sun60i_a733.c
--- a/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/dram_sun60i_a733.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/dram_sun60i_a733.c
@@ -1857,6 +1857,39 @@
 		       val, AXP8191_CHIP_ID_VAL);
 	}
 
+	/* 6b. Reset the FE1.1S USB 2.0 hub via its VBUSM input.
+	 *
+	 * U6 (FE1.1S) is strapped self-powered (BUSJ=1, R61 pull-up), so it
+	 * uses VBUSM (pin 16) as the upstream VBUS detector: a low level
+	 * makes it drop the 1.5k pull-up on DPU and restart its upstream
+	 * link state machine, even with VD33/VDD5 always present. VBUSM is
+	 * fed from USB_HOST_EN (PM5) through R59; the same PM5 also enables
+	 * U5 (VCC5V0_USB20). DCDC1/VCC_3V3_USB20HUB must NOT be cycled: it
+	 * also feeds VCC-PL and would kill the S-TWI0 bus used here.
+	 *
+	 * boot0 starts with PM5 low, so the hub sees the 0->1 edge. The
+	 * mainline SPL inherits PM5 high and never produces it. Reproduce
+	 * the edge here, while the R_PIO bank is already clocked and before
+	 * U-Boot/Linux probe the DWC3 (third PHY, USB2-DP/DM at C36/B37).
+	 */
+	{
+		void __iomem *r_pio = IOMEM(0x07025000);
+		u32 pm_cfg0, pm_dat;
+
+		/* PM5: mux = output (PM_CFG0 bits [23:20] = 0x1) */
+		pm_cfg0 = readl(r_pio + 0x20);
+		clrsetbits_le32(r_pio + 0x20, 0xf << 20, 0x1 << 20);
+
+		pm_dat = readl(r_pio + 0x40);
+		clrbits_le32(r_pio + 0x40, BIT(5));   /* VBUSM = 0, U5 off */
+		mdelay(30);                            /* hub drops DPU pull-up */
+		setbits_le32(r_pio + 0x40, BIT(5));    /* VBUSM = 1, re-attach */
+		mdelay(5);
+
+		printf("PMIC: cycled USB_HOST_EN (PM5) for FE1.1S VBUSM reset (cfg %08x, dat %08x -> %08x)\n",
+		       pm_cfg0, pm_dat, readl(r_pio + 0x40));
+	}
+
 	/* 7. LPDDR5 PMIC Sequence from running Linux / boot0 axp8191_live_regs.txt:
 	 * Sets DCDC1..9 voltages and enables, DC1SW1/2 switches, and all LDOs (BLDOs @ 1.8V for DRAM VDD1) */
 	static const struct {
